# Components, functions and connection notes

**Inventory status:** All items below are proposed candidate components, not confirmed original parts.

## Recommended student-prototype configuration

| Item | Qty. | Essential? | Purpose / selection notes |
|---|---:|---|---|
| Arduino Uno R3 | 1 | Yes | Familiar 5 V controller; sufficient pins for this basic prototype |
| TCS34725 colour sensor breakout | 1 | Yes | RGB measurement over I²C; choose a breakout compatible with the intended supply and logic levels |
| Digital IR presence sensor | 1 | Recommended | Detects tomato at sensing point; verify active output logic |
| DC geared motor | 1 | Yes | Drives belt; choose torque/speed for the load |
| Conveyor belt and frame | 1 | Yes | Mechanical transport |
| Motor driver | 1 | Yes | Must handle motor voltage and stall current; L298N is a common educational option but inefficient |
| SG90 micro servo | 1 | For lightweight gate only | Moves a small diverter; use a stronger servo/actuator if required by mechanical load |
| Start push button | 1 | Recommended | Operator start input |
| Stop push button | 1 | Recommended | Software stop input; not a safety-rated emergency stop |
| Green LED + 220–330 Ω resistor | 1 each | Optional | Running indicator |
| Red LED + 220–330 Ω resistor | 1 each | Optional | Stop/alarm indicator |
| Motor-rated DC supply | 1 | Yes | Must match motor voltage and current |
| Regulated servo supply | 1 | Recommended | Sized for servo peak current; ground referenced to controller |
| Regulated logic supply / USB | 1 | Yes | Stable power for Arduino and compatible sensor modules |
| Jumper wires / connectors | As needed | Yes | Signal wiring |
| Breadboard | 1 | Optional | Low-current prototype signals only; not for motor current |
| Mechanical brackets, fasteners and three bins | As needed | Yes | Sensor and gate mounting, collection |
| Fuse / overcurrent protection | As designed | Strongly recommended | Protects wiring and supply branches |
| Physical power disconnect / emergency-stop hardware | As designed | Strongly recommended | Provides a hardware means to remove drive power |

## Pin summary

- D2: IR output
- D3: Start button to GND (`INPUT_PULLUP`)
- D4: Stop button to GND (`INPUT_PULLUP`)
- D5: L298N ENA PWM
- D7: L298N IN1
- D8: L298N IN2
- D9: Servo signal
- D10: Green LED through resistor
- D11: Red LED through resistor
- A4: TCS34725 SDA
- A5: TCS34725 SCL

## Electrical compatibility checklist

- Confirm the colour sensor breakout voltage and I²C logic requirements.
- Confirm the IR module output voltage is safe for the Arduino input.
- Confirm motor driver current rating against motor stall current, not only free-running current.
- Do not power the motor or servo from GPIO pins.
- Do not route motor current through a breadboard.
- Ensure all signal devices have a common reference ground where needed.
- Test the supply voltage under load before connecting the Arduino.
